.TH OMX-DSP-COPY-CHECK 1 "" "omx-dsp" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
omx-dsp-copy-check \- find code that writes a libomxdsp function again
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B omx-dsp-copy-check
[\fB\-\-root\fR \fIDIR\fR] [\fB\-\-exports\fR \fIFILE\fR] [\fB\-\-allow\fR \fIFILE\fR] [\fB\-\-enforce\fR]
.br
.B omx-dsp-copy-check \-\-generate
[\fB\-\-version\fR \fIV\fR] \fIOMXDSP_TREE\fR
.br
.B omx-dsp-copy-check \-\-self\-test
[\fB\-\-sabotage\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run it at the root of a project that uses libomxdsp. It reads the tracked C and
TypeScript or JavaScript sources and prints one line for each place where the
project defines a libomxdsp name, shares most of the body of a libomxdsp
function, uses two of its constants together with its maths calls, or writes
one of its short expressions inline, such as a decibel conversion. Tests,
fakes, fixtures, oracles and generated directories are left out.
.PP
The list of what the library exports is a data file installed with the
library, \fI/usr/share/omxdsp/omx-dsp-exports.json\fR. The command looks for it
next to itself, in the \fIexports\fR variable of the \fIomxdsp.pc\fR file and in
the standard share directories.
.PP
A copy that has to stay is listed in the file \fIomx-dsp-copies.allow\fR at the
root of the project, one line per copy in the form
\fIpath:function | export | reason | issue\fR. The check fails on an entry that
no longer matches a copy and on an entry without a reason or an issue.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-root " DIR"
The project to scan. The default is the current directory.
.TP
.BI \-\-exports " FILE"
The exports file to read instead of the installed one.
.TP
.BI \-\-allow " FILE"
The allowlist to read instead of \fIomx-dsp-copies.allow\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-enforce
Exit with status 1 when a copy is not on the allowlist or the allowlist has a
stale or incomplete entry. Without it the command only reports and exits 0.
.TP
.B \-\-generate
Write the exports file for the headers and sources of a libomxdsp tree to
standard output. The library's own build does this.
.TP
.B \-\-self\-test
From a libomxdsp source tree, plant copies in a scratch project and require
each to be found and each legitimate use to pass. With \fB\-\-sabotage\fR it
breaks each rule in turn and requires the self-test to fail.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/omxdsp/omx-dsp-exports.json
The exports file.
.TP
.I omx-dsp-copies.allow
The allowlist, in the project root.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when the run finished (in report mode whatever it found), 1 when
\fB\-\-enforce\fR found a problem, 2 when the exports file could not be found or read.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pkg-config (1)
